The file containing the password to the next level is in the home Dir.
But it is named '-' which makes it hard to just 'cat' the file because - is used to indicate 
options in linux.

It is important to specify the relative path to get the contents.

in linux: 
. -> represents the current dir.
.. -> represents the dir above the current one(Parent dir of current dir).
./ -> inside of the current dir.

cat ./- yeild us the password but cat ./ - becuase the latter would be interpreted as an option 
inside of the current dir (options for cat).



